    {
      "text": "Knots, Perturbative Series and Quantum Modularity — We introduce an invariant of a hyperbolic knot which is a map α 7→Φα(h) from Q/Z to matrices with entries in Q[[h]] and with rows and columns\n\n**Knots, Perturbative Series and Quantum Modularity**\n\n*SIGMA 20 (2024), 055, 87 pages*\n\n87 pp, 48 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We introduce an invariant of a hyperbolic knot which is a map α 7→Φα(h) from Q/Z to matrices with entries in Q[[h]] and with rows and columns indexed by the boundary parabolic SL2(C) representations of the fundamental group of the knot.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Part 0: Introduction and overview; Part I: The main story; 1 The original quantum modularity conjecture; 2 A collection of formal power series; 2.1 The indexing set P_K; 2.2 Four constructions of the power series Phi; 3 Interrelations among the power series Phi_a^; 3.1 The generalized quantum modularity conject; 3.2 Lifting the QMC from constant terms to pow; 3.3 Quadratic relations; 3.4 Asymptotics of the coefficients; 4 Refining the quantum modularity conjecture; 4.1 Improving the quantum modularity conjectur; 4.2 New elements of the Habiro ring; 4.3 Smoothed optimal truncation; 4.4 Strengthening the generalized quantum modu; 4.5 The refined quantum modularity conjecture",
      "lang": "en",
